@meta
id: 09-05
title: Change the rest of the line
chapter: 09
type: lesson
skills: op-motion
par: 38
minutes: 4
vscode: select from the cursor to the end of the line, then type
open: config.ts

@brief
Support mail has moved off the old domain. The config still points at it:

    supportEmail: 'billing@old-domain.example',

It should read `'billing@globex.example',` — same quotes, same trailing
comma, new address. Fix it and save.

The key is on the line already and the value is not; do not retype the
key, and do not retype the indentation.

@keys
| `c$` | change from the cursor to the end of the line |
| `C` | the same edit, one key |
| `f'` | forward to the next single quote |

@hints
Everything from the opening quote to the end of the line is going. That
is a motion you already have.
--
`c$` wipes the tail of the line and leaves you in insert mode at the end
of what remains. `C` is the same thing in one key.
--
`j`, then `f'` to land on the opening quote, then `C` and type the whole
value including its closing quote and comma.

@solution
    j f' C 'billing@globex.example', <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Retyping the value is unavoidable — it is new text. Retyping
`  supportEmail: ` would not have been, and that is the difference between
this and double-clicking the line in VS Code and starting again.

`C` is worth committing to muscle memory now. Roughly a third of all
real-world edits are "this line is right up to here, and wrong after it":
a changed argument, a new default, a different return. `C` is the key for
exactly that thought, and it reads as "change the rest".

Where `c$` comes into its own over `C` is with a count. `2C` and `c2$`
are rare, but `c` in front of any motion at all is not — you are about to
meet `c` with find motions, word counts and paragraph jumps, and every one
of them is the same two-part sentence: change, then how far.

@start config.ts
export const config = {
  supportEmail: 'billing@old-domain.example',
  refundWindowDays: 30,
  retryLimit: 5,
};

@expected config.ts
export const config = {
  supportEmail: 'billing@globex.example',
  refundWindowDays: 30,
  retryLimit: 5,
};
